   <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Created By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/the-legend-of-zelda/shigeru-miyamoto\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Shigeru Miyamoto\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Miyamoto created The Legend of Zelda.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Created By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/the-legend-of-zelda/takashi-tezuka\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Takashi Tezuka\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Tezuka co-created The Legend of Zelda.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"topic-section\">\n    <details>\n        <summary class=\"topic-summary\">\n            <span class=\"topic-title\">Produced By</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">1</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Produced By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/the-legend-of-zelda/nintendo\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Nintendo\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Nintendo develops and publishes Zelda.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"did-you-know\">\n    <h2>Did you know?</h2>\n    <ul>\n        <li>The Legend of Zelda is also referenced as Zelda, LoZ, TLoZ.</li><li>Miyamoto created The Legend of Zelda.</li><li>Nintendo develops and publishes Zelda.</li><li>Ocarina of Time is a landmark Zelda game.</li><li>Breath of the Wild is a modern Zelda game.</li><li>Evidence around The Legend of Zelda is classified as fiction on Ton-o-Lore.</li>\n    </ul>\n</section>","overview":"<section class=\"overview\">\n    <h2>What is The Legend of Zelda?</h2>\n    \n    <p>\n        3DS Virtual Console release (Ambassador Program)\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        <a href=\"/the-legend-of-zelda/nintendo\" class=\"entity-link\">Nintendo</a> Switch Online (Living the life of luxury!)\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        (sometimes called &quot;Zelda 1&quot; or &quot;Original Zelda&quot; by fans) is an action-adventure game developed and published by <a href=\"/the-legend-of-zelda/nintendo\" class=\"entity-link\">Nintendo</a>, originally released on February 21, 1986 for the Famicom Disk System in Japan and internationally on the <a href=\"/the-legend-of-zelda/nintendo\" class=\"entity-link\">Nintendo</a> Entertainment System in 1987. It is the titular launch title of The Legend of Zelda series. The game&#039;s plot centers around a young swordsman adventurer in green named , to protect the fantasy Kingdom of Hyrule from the evil porcine-like monster Ganon who plans to rule it by force, rescue Princess Zelda, and claim the Triforce to restore peace, which would become the central theme for the currently long-running franchise. Like most other early Zelda games, it has since been re-released multiple times for several platforms, including the <a href=\"/the-legend-of-zelda/nintendo\" class=\"entity-link\">Nintendo</a> GameCube, the Game Boy Advance, as well as the Virtual Console and <a href=\"/the-legend-of-zelda/nintendo\" class=\"entity-link\">Nintendo</a> Switch Online. The Japanese version of the game is known as The Hyrule Fantasy: The Legend of Zelda.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        A breakthrough game of its age not unlike its contemporary Super Mario Bros., as this NES title is the first installment - therefore the one that debuted a majorly successful series that since became one of <a href=\"/the-legend-of-zelda/nintendo\" class=\"entity-link\">Nintendo</a>&#039;s flagship franchises (alongside Mario and Pokémon) and popularized the 2D action-adventure genre, The Legend of Zelda is widely considered one of the most important and influential video games ever created, and was highly popular during its release, selling 6.5 million copies worldwide. For a time, it was the best-selling Zelda game until Ocarina of Time on the <a href=\"/the-legend-of-zelda/nintendo\" class=\"entity-link\">Nintendo</a> 64 (which repeated its revolution for 3D) in 1998, selling 7.6 million. Therefore, it held the record for 12 years.\n    </p>\n    \n    <p class=\"also-known-as\">\n        <strong>Also known as:</strong>\n        Zelda, LoZ, TLoZ, Legend of Zelda.\n    </p>\n\n</section>","word_count":1089,"uniqueness_score":"1.0000"},"entity":{"id":"dee5eb5a-3efa-4a8b-bf77-bc0062f2469d","name":"The Legend of Zelda","slug":"the-legend-of-zelda","type":"topic","kind":"topic","type_label":"Topic","short_description":"3DS Virtual Console release (Ambassador Program)","description":"3DS Virtual Console release (Ambassador Program)\n\nNintendo Switch Online (Living the life of luxury!)\n\n(sometimes called \"Zelda 1\" or \"Original Zelda\" by fans) is an action-adventure game developed and published by Nintendo, originally released on February 21, 1986 for the Famicom Disk System in Japan and internationally on the Nintendo Entertainment System in 1987. It is the titular launch title of The Legend of Zelda series. The game's plot centers around a young swordsman adventurer in green named , to protect the fantasy Kingdom of Hyrule from the evil porcine-like monster Ganon who plans to rule it by force, rescue Princess Zelda, and claim the Triforce to restore peace, which would become the central theme for the currently long-running franchise. Like most other early Zelda games, it has since been re-released multiple times for several platforms, including the Nintendo GameCube, the Game Boy Advance, as well as the Virtual Console and Nintendo Switch Online. The Japanese version of the game is known as The Hyrule Fantasy: The Legend of Zelda.\n\nA breakthrough game of its age not unlike its contemporary Super Mario Bros., as this NES title is the first installment - therefore the one that debuted a majorly successful series that since became one of Nintendo's flagship franchises (alongside Mario and Pokémon) and popularized the 2D action-adventure genre, The Legend of Zelda is widely considered one of the most important and influential video games ever created, and was highly popular during its release, selling 6.5 million copies worldwide. For a time, it was the best-selling Zelda game until Ocarina of Time on the Nintendo 64 (which repeated its revolution for 3D) in 1998, selling 7.6 million. Therefore, it held the record for 12 years.","evidence":"fiction","universe":"the-legend-of-zelda","aliases":["Zelda","LoZ","TLoZ","Legend of Zelda"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":null,"image_source":null,"image_credit":null,"image_license":null,"image_usage":null,"image_alt":null},"connections":[],"rabbit_holes":[],"copyright":{"theme":"the-legend-of-zelda","title":"The Legend of Zelda is not owned by Ton-o-Lore.","body":"The Legend of Zelda, its characters, artwork, logos, and related intellectual property are the property of their respective rights holders, including Nintendo Co., Ltd. and other credited rights holders. Ton-o-Lore is an independent, unofficial fan and informational project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Nintendo or those rights holders. Identification logos and thumbnails, when shown, are low-resolution images used under a fair-use rationale for commentary and identification only — not free or redistributable artwork."},"subject":{"id":"the-legend-of-zelda","name":"The Legend of Zelda"